THOUGHT: The original dereference error at line 706 is gone, but my change caused two new NullAway errors where `obtain(...)` is considered nullable when passed to `action(...)`. To keep the method contract and avoid further changes, I should make `action(AnimationDesc, float)` accept a nullable `AnimationDesc` again and perform an explicit null check at the top, then call it with a non-null reference. The simplest fix is to keep the parameter annotated `@Nullable`, add a local non-null variable after a null check, and use that variable for all subsequent dereferences and returns. This will satisfy NullAway for both the dereference and the call sites without altering other behavior. After editing, I’ll rerun the compile to confirm the total error count drops from 329 to 328.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && \
sed -i '703,717c\  /** Apply an action animation on top of the current animation. */
  protected AnimationDesc action(@Nullable final AnimationDesc anim, float transitionTime) {
    if (anim == null) throw new GdxRuntimeException("AnimationDesc cannot be null");
    final AnimationDesc nonNullAnim = anim;
    if (nonNullAnim.loopCount < 0) throw new GdxRuntimeException("An action cannot be continuous");
    if (current == null || current.loopCount == 0) animate(nonNullAnim, transitionTime);
    else {
      AnimationDesc toQueue = inAction ? null : obtain(current);
      inAction = false;
      animate(nonNullAnim, transitionTime);
      inAction = true;
      if (toQueue != null) queue(toQueue, transitionTime);
    }
    return nonNullAnim;
  }
}' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/utils/AnimationController.java && \
nl -ba gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/utils/AnimationController.java | sed -n '690,720p' && \
./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && \
grep "error: \[NullAway\]" new_build_output.log | wc -l && \
grep -n "AnimationController.java" new_build_output.log || true
```

